<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Knoydart</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Knoydart is a remote, mountainous peninsula on the west coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-highlands">Scottish Highlands</a>, between Loch Nevis and Loch Hourn. It has no road link to the rest of the road network, and its small community at Inverie is reached by boat or on foot. Its people were evicted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/highland-clearances">Highland Clearances</a> of the 1850s, and in 1999 the residents bought the estate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/knoydart.jpg" alt="Knoydart" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Subarite · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverie_Knoydart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
